# WLISTTT.KEY - the jumps' requests, a failed survey, Esc stopping a jump,
# a move, repeated moves and a survey, and a count carried to a list with
# a lead row, over the eleven rows of WLLONG.REQ;
# TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/WLISTTT.SNP.  R turns on the last busy move's ITEM
# LIST requests, the title's last number.
S START
K R
S REQS
# A jump loads the page holding its row in one request, then steps
# within it: row 7 needs the page after it too; row 2 starts its page.
K 7
S JUMP7
K 2
S JUMP2
# An Esc waiting when a jump starts stops it at its first wait, after
# the page load: the window stays on the page loaded.
K 9
K E
K 3
S ESCJUMP
# F: the Home move's page loads, its survey fails: the box, then the
# growing range, the count pending; the next busy move counts.
K F
S FAILBOX
K ENTER
S FAILED
# An Esc that a jump's step finds while the count is pending: no
# survey, the count still pending.
K E
K 7
S ESCSTEP
K N
S RECOUNT
# An End move stopped by Esc did not succeed: nothing surveyed, the
# count still pending, which Home then surveys.
K F
K ENTER
K E
K B
S ESCEND
K T
S ESCHOME
# A survey stopped by Esc leaves no count and none pending: the next
# move surveys nothing, the End move counts.
K F
K ENTER
K E
K N
S ESCSURV
K N
S NOSURV
K B
S ENDCOUNT
# SHIFT-C: the count carried to a list with a lead row, which the range
# counts and the count does not.
K SHIFT-C
S CARRYLD
K B
S CARRYEND
# CTRL-SHIFT-O: a window of one row shows no lead row.
K CTRL-SHIFT-O
S ONELEAD
K B
S ONEEND
# An Esc stops line moves repeated in one gesture at their first wait:
# only the first is made.
K T
K E
K SHIFT-D
S ESCREP
